<title>JAPAN: Nippon Credit shares bid-only in morning.</title>
<headline>Nippon Credit shares bid-only in morning.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Nippon Credit Bank Ltd (NCB) were bid-only on Friday morning, as buy-backs continued after the bank's announcement Thursday that it and Bankers Trust New York Corp had agreed on a business tie-up.</p>
<p>As of 0055 GMT, NCB were bid at 205 yen, against Thursday's close of 190 yen.</p>
<p>NCB shares had been hit hard due to worries over its financial health, even after the bank announced a restructuring plan on April 1.</p>
</text>
